    https://www.online-cpp.com/cyqB0632Ss
We can take random test case as A[ ]=1 2 1 1 3 and dry run it :-


   ->

    when we reach A[2]=1:- we will observe :-


     P = 1


   : This is because len1 contains equal values but since another distinct value(i.e 2) has arrived we cannot increment len1 and restart its counting.


   ->

    And when we reach A[4]=3:-


   we can find we cannot do len2+1 bcz 3rd distinct variable has arrived so:-


       Q = len1 + 1


     : bcz when 3rd distinct variable(i.e 3) has arrived and  we have to stop len2 counting and restart it with len1.

